Task 1: Set up GitOps Repositories for Application Configurations
Subtask 1.1: Create Application Repository Structure
First, let's create a proper GitOps repository structure for our multi-cluster application deployment.

Access your lab environment and open a terminal

Create a new directory for your GitOps repository

mkdir -p ~/multi-cluster-apps
cd ~/multi-cluster-apps
Initialize the Git repository
git init
git config user.name "Lab User"
git config user.email "labuser@example.com"
Create the directory structure for multi-cluster applications
mkdir -p {applications,clusters,overlays}/{production,staging}
mkdir -p base/sample-app
mkdir -p argocd-apps
Create the base application manifests
Create the base deployment configuration:

cat > base/sample-app/deployment.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sample-web-app
  labels:
    app: sample-web-app
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: sample-web-app
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: sample-web-app
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: web-app
        image: nginx:1.21
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "64Mi"
            cpu: "50m"
          limits:
            memory: "128Mi"
            cpu: "100m"
EOF
Create the service manifest
cat > base/sample-app/service.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: sample-web-app-service
  labels:
    app: sample-web-app
spec:
  selector:
    app: sample-web-app
  ports:
  - protocol: TCP
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
  type: ClusterIP
EOF
Create the route manifest
cat > base/sample-app/route.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: route.openshift.io/v1
kind: Route
metadata:
  name: sample-web-app-route
  labels:
    app: sample-web-app
spec:
  to:
    kind: Service
    name: sample-web-app-service
  port:
    targetPort: 80
EOF
Create the kustomization file for the base
cat > base/sample-app/kustomization.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization

resources:
- deployment.yaml
- service.yaml
- route.yaml

commonLabels:
  app.kubernetes.io/name: sample-web-app
  app.kubernetes.io/version: "1.0"
EOF
Subtask 1.2: Create Cluster-Specific Overlays
Now we'll create overlays for different clusters to demonstrate environment-specific configurations.

Create overlay for the East cluster (Production)
cat > overlays/production/kustomization.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization

namespace: production-apps

resources:
- ../../base/sample-app

patchesStrategicMerge:
- deployment-patch.yaml

commonLabels:
  environment: production
  cluster: east
EOF
Create the deployment patch for production
cat > overlays/production/deployment-patch.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sample-web-app
spec:
  replicas: 3
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: web-app
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "128Mi"
            cpu: "100m"
          limits:
            memory: "256Mi"
            cpu: "200m"
EOF
Create overlay for the West cluster (Staging)
cat > overlays/staging/kustomization.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization

namespace: staging-apps

resources:
- ../../base/sample-app

patchesStrategicMerge:
- deployment-patch.yaml

commonLabels:
  environment: staging
  cluster: west
EOF
Create the deployment patch for staging
cat > overlays/staging/deployment-patch.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sample-web-app
spec:
  replicas: 1
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: web-app
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "32Mi"
            cpu: "25m"
          limits:
            memory: "64Mi"
            cpu: "50m"
EOF
Subtask 1.3: Create ArgoCD Application Definitions
Create ArgoCD Application for Production cluster
cat > argocd-apps/production-app.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: sample-app-production
  namespace: openshift-gitops
  labels:
    environment: production
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/your-username/multi-cluster-apps.git
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: overlays/production
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: production-apps
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
    - CreateNamespace=true
EOF
Create ArgoCD Application for Staging cluster
cat > argocd-apps/staging-app.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: sample-app-staging
  namespace: openshift-gitops
  labels:
    environment: staging
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/your-username/multi-cluster-apps.git
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: overlays/staging
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: staging-apps
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
    - CreateNamespace=true
EOF
Commit and push the repository structure
git add .
git commit -m "Initial GitOps repository structure for multi-cluster deployment"
Note: In a real environment, you would push this to a remote Git repository. For this lab, we'll simulate this step.

Task 2: Deploy Applications Across Multiple Clusters
Subtask 2.1: Configure RHACM for Multi-Cluster Application Management
Login to the OpenShift hub cluster
oc login --server=https://api.hub-cluster.example.com:6443 --username=admin --password=admin123
Verify RHACM installation and managed clusters
oc get managedclusters
Expected output should show your managed clusters:

NAME           HUB ACCEPTED   MANAGED CLUSTER URLS   JOINED   AVAILABLE   AGE
cluster-east   true                                  True     True        2d
cluster-west   true                                  True     True        2d
local-cluster  true                                  True     True        2d
Create namespaces for application deployment
oc create namespace multi-cluster-apps
oc create namespace production-apps
oc create namespace staging-apps
Subtask 2.2: Create RHACM Application Resources
Create a Channel resource for Git repository
cat > channel.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Channel
metadata:
  name: multi-cluster-apps-channel
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
spec:
  type: Git
  pathname: https://github.com/your-username/multi-cluster-apps.git
  secretRef:
    name: git-secret
EOF
Apply the Channel resource
oc apply -f channel.yaml
Create PlacementRule for Production clusters
cat > placement-production.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: production-placement
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: production
  clusterReplicas: 1
EOF
Create PlacementRule for Staging clusters
cat > placement-staging.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: PlacementRule
metadata:
  name: staging-placement
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
spec:
  clusterSelector:
    matchLabels:
      environment: staging
  clusterReplicas: 1
EOF
Apply the PlacementRule resources
oc apply -f placement-production.yaml
oc apply -f placement-staging.yaml
Subtask 2.3: Create RHACM Applications
Create the Production Application
cat > application-production.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: app.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: sample-app-production
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
spec:
  componentKinds:
  - group: apps.open-cluster-management.io
    kind: Subscription
  descriptor: {}
  selector:
    matchExpressions:
    - key: app
      operator: In
      values:
      - sample-app-production
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: sample-app-production-subscription
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
  labels:
    app: sample-app-production
  annotations:
    apps.open-cluster-management.io/git-path: overlays/production
    apps.open-cluster-management.io/git-branch: main
spec:
  channel: multi-cluster-apps/multi-cluster-apps-channel
  placement:
    placementRef:
      name: production-placement
      kind: PlacementRule
EOF
Create the Staging Application
cat > application-staging.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: app.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: sample-app-staging
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
spec:
  componentKinds:
  - group: apps.open-cluster-management.io
    kind: Subscription
  descriptor: {}
  selector:
    matchExpressions:
    - key: app
      operator: In
      values:
      - sample-app-staging
---
apiVersion: apps.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: sample-app-staging-subscription
  namespace: multi-cluster-apps
  labels:
    app: sample-app-staging
  annotations:
    apps.open-cluster-management.io/git-path: overlays/staging
    apps.open-cluster-management.io/git-branch: main
spec:
  channel: multi-cluster-apps/multi-cluster-apps-channel
  placement:
    placementRef:
      name: staging-placement
      kind: PlacementRule
EOF
Deploy the applications
oc apply -f application-production.yaml
oc apply -f application-staging.yaml
Subtask 2.4: Label Managed Clusters for Proper Placement
Label the East cluster for production
oc label managedcluster cluster-east environment=production
Label the West cluster for staging
oc label managedcluster cluster-west environment=staging
Verify cluster labels
oc get managedclusters --show-labels
