Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Application Not Deploying to Target Clusters
Symptoms: Subscriptions show as created but applications don't appear on managed clusters.

Solution:

# Check placement rule status
oc describe placementrule production-placement -n multi-cluster-apps

# Verify cluster labels match placement rule selectors
oc get managedclusters --show-labels

# Check subscription events
oc describe subscription sample-app-production-subscription -n multi-cluster-apps
Issue 2: Git Repository Access Issues
Symptoms: Channel shows connection errors or authentication failures.

Solution:

# Verify channel status
oc describe channel multi-cluster-apps-channel -n multi-cluster-apps

# Check if git secret exists and is properly configured
oc get secrets -n multi-cluster-apps | grep git
Issue 3: Resource Conflicts
Symptoms: Applications fail to deploy due to existing resources.

Solution:

# Clean up existing resources
oc delete all -l app=sample-web-app -n production-apps
oc delete all -l app=sample-web-app -n staging-apps

# Redeploy applications
oc delete subscription sample-app-production-subscription -n multi-cluster-apps
oc delete subscription sample-app-staging-subscription -n multi-cluster-apps
oc apply -f application-production.yaml
oc apply -f application-staging.yaml
Best Practices for Multi-Cluster Application Deployment
1. Repository Structure
Use clear directory structures separating base configurations from overlays
Implement proper branching strategies (main for production, develop for staging)
Use semantic versioning for application releases
2. Security Considerations
Use separate service accounts for different environments
Implement proper RBAC policies for each cluster
Secure Git repository access with appropriate authentication
3. Monitoring and Observability
Implement health checks for all deployed applications
Set up monitoring dashboards for multi-cluster visibility
Configure alerting for application failures or inconsistencies
4. Disaster Recovery
Maintain backup strategies for application configurations
Test failover scenarios between clusters
Document recovery procedures for each environment
